@ryanvogel IMO the more automated feedback loops you give to the agent, the better it performs.

Obviously you need to structure your codebase so your tests are high-leverage and test the right things. Deep modules that hide secrets, etc

But for me they have been an invaluable tool.

@terminalxw Yeah I'm imagining that you'd run this in a single context window.

1 for implementation, 1 for reducing LOC, 1 for code review

That way the three incentives balance each other out
